        "created_at": "2015-01-22T17:17:04.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>\"To give (someone) the bird\" as in the gesture comes from the 1860s expression \"to give the big bird\" which meant to hiss at someone like a goose, and then was expanded to include catcalling and booing, like in pantomime or vaudeville. Then it got transferred to the \"up yours\" middle figure gesture we all know and love today.</p>",
