        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mrlerobot/{size}/1932_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-01-23T00:22:33.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I'll add to the expat's conversation (although I enjoyed the part about birds and Old English :) ) by mentioning the quote on WM's \"An Unwise Wager\": \"But what if you did have power? And by power, I mean all of it...\". What if Wager Master is referring to the fact that he knows that Expat has powers but is showing her what she could do if she led the Citizens of the Sun (\"all of it\" refering to the leadership of the Citizens...).</p><p>Or...</p><p>Expat have latent powers that she can't control. WM: \"What if you could finally control all your inherent power?</p><p>What I find interesting on \"An Unwise Wager\" is the fact that Expat still has the scar on her eye. If WM is showing her an alternate reality where she actually has powers, then it makes little sense for her to be missing an eye (because Expat lost her eyes basically because she didn't have powers, right?), from a timing perspective...</p>",
