      {
        "id": 128963,
        "name": "Chaosmancer",
        "username": "Chaosmancer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/chaosmancer/{size}/1977_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-01-23T07:04:41.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Wagermaster is very interesting really.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>He seems to want to give Absolute Zero everything he wants. Possibly the same with Expat.</p><p>He challenges Setback in a way that his powers perfectly combat (insane quiz sho where he wins with lucky guesses). Similiar with Wraith (an infinite maze for a detective)</p><p>He uses bad puns against Unity. (A hot iron)</p><p>A \"New Deal\" with Guise (Very interesting background I just realized, I thik they broke the 4th and 5th walls)</p><p>And freaks when the scholar offers him the philosopher's stone.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I think there are a lot of sub-text meanings and clues buried in here, especially with AbZero. Wager Master isn't interested in making a deal or anything, he just wants Zero to admit \"his friends are liars\" which means that the true goal seems to be turning the heroes against each other, seperating them. Playing each hero in a specific way.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
